Checking a type with type()
type() tells you the type of any value, and it’s priceless when a bug surprises you:

print(type(2026))       # int
print(type("Tobi"))    # str
print(type(9.99))       # float



&lt;class 'int'&gt;
&lt;class 'str'&gt;
&lt;class 'float'&gt;

